# Requirements Interpretation

The project requirements document is authoritative for business behavior.

## Requirement precedence

When requirements conflict, use this precedence:

1. Explicit current client decision
2. Updated client requirements via user request inputs
3. Approved architecture decision record
4. Current approved functional requirements
5. Original TOR implementation wording
6. AI assumptions

Never allow an AI assumption to override an explicit client decision.

## Superseded Technical References

The original TOR contains technical references that may no longer represent
the agreed implementation.

Examples include implementation-specific framework references.

Do not infer the technology stack from those references.

The current project technology baseline is defined by the project rules.



## Main Components
1 Investor onboarding & aftercare platform 
2 Certificates & anti-forgery verification (MVP) 
3 Investor-to-business matchmaking
4 External system integrations (ORC, GIS, payments)
5 AI assistant (chatbot) 
6 Internal automation & dashboards

