## Ambiguity

When a requirement is incomplete:

- do not invent business policy;
- identify the missing decision;
- document the assumption if implementation must temporarily proceed;
- keep the implementation replaceable where practical.

## Requirement Traceability

Major features should be traceable to one or more requirements.

Use identifiers such as:

FR-01
FR-02
FR-03

and

NFR-01
NFR-02
NFR-03

when discussing requirements.

Implementation plans should reference the relevant requirement identifiers.

## No Silent Requirement Changes

Do not change the meaning of a requirement simply to make implementation easier.

If implementation reveals a contradiction or infeasible requirement,
surface it explicitly.



## Confirmed Client Decisions Beyond the Original TOR

The original TOR is not the sole source of current business behavior.

Current explicit client decisions supersede conflicting or less-specific TOR
wording.

A confirmed client decision currently establishes that:

- investors must register;
- investors must verify email;
- investors must verify phone;
- verified investors receive authenticated investor dashboard access;
- only approved and active opportunities are available to investors;
- investors may review eligible opportunities;
- investors may make inquiries and/or express interest;
- authorized management personnel review investor interactions;
- management actions are permission-controlled;
- subsequent workflow behavior must follow confirmed business rules.

These requirements are authoritative even where the original TOR describes
opportunities as publicly discoverable.

Do not revert to public unrestricted opportunity access because of older TOR
wording.

Do not invent the downstream investor interaction workflow where the client
has not yet specified it.


## Confirmed Client Decisions

The following are confirmed requirements even where the original TOR does not
describe them with sufficient detail:

### Investor registration and protected opportunity access

The platform shall provide investor registration and onboarding.

An investor must successfully verify their required contact channels,
including email and phone, before receiving the applicable authenticated
investor access.

Authenticated and successfully onboarded investors shall have access to their
investor dashboard.

Eligible approved/active investment opportunities shall be made available to
eligible authenticated investors through the investor experience.

Investors may review eligible opportunities and initiate an inquiry and/or
expression of interest.

Management personnel with the appropriate role and permission shall review
resulting investor engagements and continue the applicable approval/review
workflow.

This requirement takes precedence over any earlier discovery interpretation
that treated authenticated investor access or investor onboarding as
unconfirmed or out of scope.

### Requirement evolution

The original TOR is not assumed to contain every current production/client
decision.

Where an explicit current client decision supplied through project
requirements supersedes or expands the TOR, the current client decision takes
precedence.

Such changes must be reflected in:

- requirements documentation;
- traceability;
- relevant ADRs;
- implementation plans;
- automated tests.

Do not silently discard an original TOR requirement. Where the newer client
decision changes its meaning, record the relationship explicitly.
